WEBVTT

00:01.300 --> 00:02.980
I heard from the person directly.

00:03.380 --> 00:05.260
Mimimi confessed to you, right?

00:05.960 --> 00:08.950
Yes. I'm sorry for hiding it from you.

00:09.500 --> 00:10.670
Well, that's okay.

00:10.670 --> 00:11.910
For now,

00:12.470 --> 00:17.550
I guess Fuuka is going to be
your main event from now on.

00:17.910 --> 00:18.260
MINAMI NANAMI

00:18.260 --> 00:19.120
MINAMI NANAMI
Because you've reached

00:19.120 --> 00:20.550
MINAMI NANAMI
your goal on Mimimi's map.

00:20.920 --> 00:23.920
You're saying "goal" again...

00:23.920 --> 00:26.300
But if you want to do that,

00:26.300 --> 00:26.690
MINAMI NANAMI

00:26.690 --> 00:28.470
MINAMI NANAMI
you can go ahead and fill up

00:28.470 --> 00:29.690
MINAMI NANAMI
Mimimi's side event.

00:31.560 --> 00:33.220
Eh? Is that so?

00:34.220 --> 00:36.700
You like to challenge yourself

00:37.510 --> 00:39.680
according to what you want to do, right?

00:53.950 --> 01:04.209
BOTTOM-TIER CHARACTER TOMOZAKI
2ND STAGE

02:10.990 --> 02:11.930
LV.10: THE PATTERNS ENGRAVED ON THE TABLET
ARE CONNECTED TO THE MYSTERIES OF THE WORLD

02:11.930 --> 02:12.990
Well, then, first,

02:13.540 --> 02:15.490
let's decide on the cast for our play.

02:15.490 --> 02:15.990
PERFORMERS - LIBRA - CHRIS

02:15.990 --> 02:17.740
PERFORMERS - LIBRA - CHRIS
First, let's start with the lead role, Libra.

02:18.270 --> 02:19.490
What kind of character is he?

02:19.800 --> 02:22.960
Libra is good at
getting close to people.

02:23.310 --> 02:26.750
He is attentive, smart, and curious.

02:27.240 --> 02:29.350
That role is suitable for me, right?!

02:29.630 --> 02:32.630
TAKEI: 1 VOTE, HASHI: 10 VOTES,
MIZUSAWA: 23 VOTES

02:32.920 --> 02:34.530
It's decided for Takahiro!

02:34.530 --> 02:36.760
Eh? Why?!

02:38.260 --> 02:43.080
Well, I'm not sure
if I'm the right person for the role,

02:43.080 --> 02:45.770
but since I've been chosen, I'll do it.

02:45.770 --> 02:46.290
CHRIS - ARCIA

02:46.290 --> 02:47.900
CHRIS - ARCIA
Next is Chris.

02:48.230 --> 02:50.760
Chris is a scared but innocent girl.

02:51.470 --> 02:53.650
She's a little childish.

02:53.650 --> 02:56.660
SENO: 5 VOTES,
KASHIWAZAKI: 9 VOTES, NATSUBAYASHI: 20 VOTES

02:56.950 --> 02:58.780
It's decided for Tama!

02:59.070 --> 03:01.290
Okay, I'll do my best.

03:01.570 --> 03:03.560
The last one for the main role is Arcia.

03:04.230 --> 03:07.040
She's a perfect girl who's
brilliant and quick-witted,

03:07.040 --> 03:09.920
and everyone relies on her.

03:12.710 --> 03:15.210
We know who's fit for that role, right?

03:16.410 --> 03:19.680
I guess I'll have to run for it, right?

03:19.680 --> 03:20.090
LIBRA: MIZUSAWA - CHRIS: NATSUBAYASHI

03:20.090 --> 03:21.930
ARCIA: HINAMI
Then it's decided for Aoi!

03:22.300 --> 03:25.440
Let's give applause to the three of them
who are taking on the main roles!

03:26.940 --> 03:27.460
Congrats!

03:27.460 --> 03:29.080
- I look forward to your play!
- Give your best!

03:29.940 --> 03:30.250
PLAY
PERFORMERS:

03:30.250 --> 03:30.690
LIBRA - MIZUSAWA
Okay.

03:30.690 --> 03:31.210
CHRIS - NATSUBAYASHI
Okay.

03:31.210 --> 03:31.950
ARCIA - HINAMI
this is how the roles of the play

03:31.950 --> 03:32.680
NARRATION: YUZU
this is how the roles of the play

03:32.680 --> 03:33.400
DIRECTOR: TOMOZAKI
and the manga cafe will be divided.

03:33.400 --> 03:33.960
SCRIPT: KIKUCHI
and the manga cafe will be divided.

03:33.960 --> 03:34.530
DIRECTOR: TOMOZAKI
and the manga cafe will be divided.

03:34.530 --> 03:36.950
MANGA CAFE

03:37.830 --> 03:40.480
Thank you very much, Tomozaki.

03:41.970 --> 03:44.650
I'm really happy right now.

03:44.650 --> 03:46.580
Once we decided
who would play the role,

03:46.850 --> 03:48.760
I started to get more and more ideas.

03:49.370 --> 03:50.060
I see.

03:50.600 --> 03:52.040
Brain!

03:52.750 --> 03:55.090
I think it's time for us
to have a meeting too,

03:55.090 --> 03:57.340
or we won't make it!

03:57.630 --> 04:00.090
Oh, that's right...
Stand-up comedy, right?

04:00.370 --> 04:04.540
That's right, Brain!
You forgot?

04:04.540 --> 04:06.350
Sorry, I've been a little busy lately.

04:06.730 --> 04:09.830
Well, you have to direct the play too.

04:09.830 --> 04:15.070
Let's say, how about we do that
after school today?

04:15.340 --> 04:17.019
Are you planning on something?

04:17.720 --> 04:19.779
Is that fine with you, Kikuchi?

04:20.730 --> 04:22.230
Ah, yes...

04:25.720 --> 04:28.220
N-Now, what shall we do?

04:28.520 --> 04:31.130
Y-You're right...

04:31.390 --> 04:33.750
D-Do you have any ideas?

04:34.060 --> 04:35.050
Umm...

04:35.370 --> 04:39.970
I was thinking of something
like a couple comedy...

04:40.220 --> 04:41.720
A-A couple?

04:42.090 --> 04:45.470
But, well, I thought about
something else too...

04:45.760 --> 04:47.700
Oh, I see...

04:49.970 --> 04:50.980
Say...

04:52.420 --> 04:55.320
You know, I said it to you, didn't I?

04:55.610 --> 04:57.990
About what?

04:58.770 --> 05:00.130
"I like you."

05:00.760 --> 05:02.120
Ah, yeah.

05:02.670 --> 05:05.530
What did you think

05:05.950 --> 05:08.370
when I said that to you?

05:08.970 --> 05:10.120
Well...

05:10.850 --> 05:12.840
I'm happy, really happy.

05:13.670 --> 05:14.230
I see.

05:15.500 --> 05:16.950
But to be honest,

05:17.450 --> 05:22.230
I myself don't know
what to do from there.

05:23.470 --> 05:24.730
I see.

05:24.730 --> 05:27.390
But, you know, maybe you're...

05:29.400 --> 05:32.790
I mean, is it okay with you?
Am I troubling you somehow?

05:32.790 --> 05:35.330
N-No, it's fine.

05:43.030 --> 05:45.410
If so, that's fine.

05:45.770 --> 05:46.940
Yeah...

05:49.820 --> 05:50.680
So...

05:52.660 --> 05:57.420
Mimimi, what do you think it means
for a guy and a girl to be in a relationship?

05:57.770 --> 06:00.420
That's so sudden!
A guy and a girl?!

06:00.420 --> 06:01.810
That's right!

06:01.810 --> 06:03.680
I mean, I want to know
the reason why.

06:05.220 --> 06:07.680
Can I take this seriously?

06:07.980 --> 06:09.430
Of course.

06:10.070 --> 06:13.290
I told you before that I'm not
a standout in any way

06:13.290 --> 06:16.690
and that I can't be special

06:17.050 --> 06:18.550
unless I became number one, right?

06:19.250 --> 06:22.160
I know I shouldn't think like that,

06:22.160 --> 06:24.160
but it's hard to change something

06:24.160 --> 06:26.020
that is so deeply rooted in your mind.

06:26.460 --> 06:30.830
But you gave me the chance
to change that.

06:31.630 --> 06:33.310
You mean the election?

06:33.310 --> 06:34.210
That's right.

06:34.490 --> 06:36.610
And with Tama and Erika's case,

06:37.030 --> 06:38.210
well, about everything.

06:39.240 --> 06:41.840
I couldn't do anything about it,

06:41.840 --> 06:44.730
but you solved it like
you're changing the world.

06:45.160 --> 06:48.370
You're the person I wanted to be,

06:48.680 --> 06:51.970
but also the person I couldn't be.

06:52.940 --> 06:54.230
So,

06:54.710 --> 06:57.730
my confession was also
a spur-of-the-moment thing at first,

06:57.730 --> 07:00.150
but when I think about it,

07:00.710 --> 07:03.240
I realize that it was
the same thing after all.

07:03.580 --> 07:04.410
The same thing?

07:05.280 --> 07:07.110
That is...

07:07.660 --> 07:09.640
...I really like you, Tomozaki.

07:12.500 --> 07:14.310
That's the reason

07:14.650 --> 07:17.930
why I thought you were good for me.

07:19.160 --> 07:22.250
Wait! Am I troubling you again?!

07:22.250 --> 07:25.010
N-No, it's not.

07:25.450 --> 07:27.000
Oh, geez!

07:27.000 --> 07:30.510
I'm so embarrassed,
so forget what I said here!

07:30.780 --> 07:31.220
Eh?

07:31.530 --> 07:32.770
O-Okay.

07:33.060 --> 07:37.190
However! I'll be sad
if you forget everything, so no!

07:37.800 --> 07:39.400
What does that mean?

07:39.400 --> 07:41.880
The maiden's heart is hard
to understand, you know?

07:41.880 --> 07:42.890
I-I see...

07:43.380 --> 07:44.670
It's difficult...

07:45.670 --> 07:47.280
Well then, Brain!

07:47.610 --> 07:49.440
I hope you sleep well tonight!

07:50.550 --> 07:51.600
Hey...

07:52.050 --> 07:54.290
What about practicing
our stand-up comedy?

07:54.290 --> 07:56.290
TOMOZAKI

07:59.720 --> 08:01.400
That's the reason

08:01.880 --> 08:05.380
why I thought you were good for me.

08:06.170 --> 08:08.880
I'm wondering...

08:09.620 --> 08:11.270
where's the 'special reason' for me?

08:13.670 --> 08:15.140
Tomozaki, here.

08:15.140 --> 08:15.460
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF

08:15.460 --> 08:17.050
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF
Since the cast has been decided,

08:17.050 --> 08:18.890
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF
I tried to adjust the lines.

08:19.180 --> 08:20.720
Eh? In one night?

08:20.720 --> 08:23.910
Yes. But I haven't worked
on the last scene.

08:29.540 --> 08:32.700
She changed a lot of things,
not just the lines.

08:34.080 --> 08:36.860
Chris has been taking care
of flying dragon all her life

08:37.240 --> 08:39.409
and has never been outside the garden.

08:39.799 --> 08:41.500
She is such a sad little girl.

08:42.980 --> 08:45.920
But the garden had everything.

08:46.650 --> 08:48.000
Soft beds,

08:49.000 --> 08:50.550
clean water,

08:51.550 --> 08:52.990
warm baths,

08:54.140 --> 08:56.410
books of myths and fairy tales to read,

08:57.230 --> 09:00.000
and the same food as royalty.

09:01.560 --> 09:03.470
Except for those things,

09:03.850 --> 09:06.070
the garden didn't have anything else.

09:08.600 --> 09:11.110
The first change was
the scene of their encounter.

09:12.060 --> 09:14.120
Chris, who had lived a solitary life,

09:14.120 --> 09:15.720
knowing neither joy nor sorrow,

09:16.010 --> 09:18.010
met Libra and Arcia for the first time.

09:18.290 --> 09:20.080
In the first script,

09:20.080 --> 09:21.760
Chris had this reaction:

09:23.750 --> 09:25.790
Another human than me?

09:26.320 --> 09:28.090
Hey, I'm Chris.

09:28.390 --> 09:29.940
What are your names?

09:30.990 --> 09:34.010
That was Chris's curiosity
about the outside

09:34.010 --> 09:35.600
and her straightforwardness.

09:36.120 --> 09:38.850
But in the rewritten script...

09:39.460 --> 09:42.190
Another human than me?

09:42.490 --> 09:45.650
W-Who are you?
What do you want here?

09:46.290 --> 09:49.300
She was alert and frightened.

09:49.740 --> 09:52.180
Chris was hoping for relief from loneliness,

09:52.530 --> 09:55.960
but more than that, she was afraid
of the unknown world and change.

09:56.970 --> 10:00.130
Also, unlike the first script,

10:00.130 --> 10:02.230
Libra was no longer a simple hero.

10:03.030 --> 10:05.160
He had changed into a life-sized boy

10:05.160 --> 10:07.930
who was clumsy
and made many mistakes,

10:08.360 --> 10:10.470
but he gained friends
through his perseverance.

10:11.380 --> 10:14.930
In other words, both of them were
emphasizing their "weakness."

10:16.110 --> 10:18.970
However, only Arcia was different.

10:19.720 --> 10:20.610
For example,

10:20.610 --> 10:23.350
in the scene when she encounters
Chris and a flying dragon.

10:23.350 --> 10:28.610
In the first script, Arcia senses danger
and tries to escape,

10:29.500 --> 10:31.240
but in the rewritten script...

10:31.800 --> 10:32.900
Libra, stay back!

10:33.540 --> 10:37.610
Arcia quickly moves to break
the dragon's wings herself.

10:38.150 --> 10:41.510
If she did so, it was her own fault
that the flying dragon could no longer fly.

10:42.070 --> 10:45.830
It would not matter if Libra
was an impurity or not.

10:46.400 --> 10:49.160
But Libra notices and stops her.

10:49.160 --> 10:50.220
What are you doing?

10:50.730 --> 10:52.190
I'm royalty,

10:52.190 --> 10:54.850
and I'm not going to be executed
unless I do something wrong.

10:55.400 --> 10:57.480
So let me do it.

10:58.300 --> 10:59.670
But, Arcia...

11:00.130 --> 11:02.470
Your heart will die!

11:06.890 --> 11:08.730
Thanks to Arcia's bluff,

11:09.270 --> 11:11.350
Libra escapes the execution.

11:12.010 --> 11:15.130
The story then shifts to the relationship

11:15.130 --> 11:17.160
between the three of them in the garden.

11:18.080 --> 11:21.320
Given the roles of caretaker and educator,

11:21.650 --> 11:24.360
the three of them developed a warm
and mysterious relationship,

11:24.360 --> 11:27.020
like that of friends and family.

11:28.000 --> 11:30.630
Chris likes to make flower decorations

11:30.970 --> 11:32.670
and read books.

11:33.270 --> 11:35.980
But to avoid the "impurity"
of the secular world,

11:35.980 --> 11:38.390
she is only allowed to read
myths and fairy tales.

11:39.290 --> 11:41.680
She had read all the books
in the castle's library,

11:42.010 --> 11:43.760
and the next thing she was hooked on were

11:43.760 --> 11:46.330
the stories Libra told her about
the outside of the castle.

11:46.970 --> 11:50.570
Actually, the fastest of all dragons
is the giant dragon.

11:51.090 --> 11:54.820
They really fly at great speed.

11:54.820 --> 11:57.450
Really? And so?

11:57.930 --> 12:02.570
Recently, there have been facilities that use
this power to generate magical power.

12:03.110 --> 12:07.080
They say that converting physical power
into magic is a great invention!

12:07.080 --> 12:08.940
Wow, that's great!

12:09.330 --> 12:13.490
By the way, there's one magic
I'm good at too.

12:13.490 --> 12:15.340
It's called "unlock."

12:16.550 --> 12:18.950
Isn't that the power of physics?

12:19.290 --> 12:22.100
It's not magic because
you just unlock locks, right?

12:22.870 --> 12:23.760
So you knew it?

12:24.160 --> 12:27.690
What Libra tells her is
a story about the real world.

12:27.690 --> 12:28.880
Where the people live,

12:28.880 --> 12:31.350
sometimes they fight,
love each other,

12:31.720 --> 12:33.040
and die.

12:33.990 --> 12:39.240
But, you know, with this one thing,
I can go places and see things.

12:39.540 --> 12:42.700
That's why I think it's all I need.

12:43.320 --> 12:46.500
I see. So, your unlocking magic...

12:48.320 --> 12:51.000
...is very nice magic, isn't it?

12:51.450 --> 12:52.910
Arcia, on the other hand,

12:52.910 --> 12:57.070
was so brilliant and hardworking
that she won many magic competitions.

12:57.070 --> 13:00.260
And she was always strict
when she taught Chris.

13:00.610 --> 13:04.440
So the idea that non-royalty
is impure is just a myth,

13:04.440 --> 13:05.590
with no basis in fact.

13:06.030 --> 13:09.770
That is an old-fashioned custom
in aristocratic society.

13:10.050 --> 13:12.280
That's scary...

13:12.280 --> 13:15.530
Isn't there anything more fun to learn?

13:15.530 --> 13:18.150
Maybe some fun stories
about the outside world?

13:19.850 --> 13:22.410
Let's see. Chris, do you know
what a butterfly is?

13:22.900 --> 13:25.910
Eh? Butterflies are insects, right?

13:26.280 --> 13:27.600
Like this one, right?

13:28.260 --> 13:29.920
That's a woodlouse.

13:29.920 --> 13:32.240
It's an insect, but it's not
the same as a butterfly.

13:32.520 --> 13:35.420
But this is the only insect
around here, right?

13:35.770 --> 13:37.630
That's why you need to study.

13:38.110 --> 13:41.930
You need basic knowledge
to hear what's out there.

13:42.210 --> 13:44.990
I feel like I'm being cooped up.

13:44.990 --> 13:46.790
Oh, it's like the woodlouse!

13:47.450 --> 13:50.430
Okay, then, open the last
lesson I taught you.

13:50.430 --> 13:52.190
Ignore?

13:52.190 --> 13:53.810
Ah, I just ignore it!

13:53.810 --> 13:56.820
Alright, let's continue our last lesson.

13:59.180 --> 14:00.280
...once in a while!

14:00.790 --> 14:02.360
Ah, I just ignore it!

14:03.020 --> 14:05.560
Tama really suits Chris' character.

14:06.760 --> 14:12.390
And that person's other persona
really suits this Arcia's character.

14:13.560 --> 14:17.040
The turning point in this story
was the flying dragon.

14:17.830 --> 14:20.840
Flying dragons are creatures that
are able to fly by the age of 13.

14:21.260 --> 14:22.010
In other words,

14:22.010 --> 14:24.110
a dragon that could not fly by then

14:24.110 --> 14:27.550
would have lost the power
to fly due to "impurity."

14:28.310 --> 14:31.710
The flying dragon Chris is raising
is 13 years old this year.

14:32.020 --> 14:33.400
But it was still unable to fly.

14:34.090 --> 14:37.900
I wonder what kind of "impurity"
is preventing it from flying.

14:39.320 --> 14:40.690
Chris, did you know?

14:41.560 --> 14:44.550
Flying dragons can read people's minds.

14:45.050 --> 14:46.200
People's mind?

14:46.530 --> 14:48.300
And flying dragons are kind.

14:48.790 --> 14:52.200
They never forget the debt of gratitude
they owe to the people who raised them.

14:52.630 --> 14:56.210
They try to fulfill their wishes
as much as possible.

14:57.080 --> 14:58.450
That means...

14:59.600 --> 15:00.330
Say...

15:00.970 --> 15:01.780
You don't want...

15:03.610 --> 15:06.490
...to fly, do you?

15:07.340 --> 15:09.440
What was revealed in this way

15:09.440 --> 15:10.970
was Chris' weakness.

15:11.990 --> 15:13.530
Everything was in the garden,

15:14.020 --> 15:15.510
and only those things.

15:16.850 --> 15:18.120
That's why she was lonely

15:18.400 --> 15:20.070
and wished to go outside.

15:20.590 --> 15:24.500
But now that she has "everything,"
Chris' fear of the unknown world

15:25.000 --> 15:27.640
outweighs her desire to leave the garden

15:27.640 --> 15:30.520
and spread her wings.

15:31.590 --> 15:32.090
Yes...

15:32.740 --> 15:36.000
It was her heart that bound...

15:36.750 --> 15:39.130
...the wings of the flying dragon.

15:40.000 --> 15:42.000
BOTTOM-TIER CHARACTER TOMOZAKI
2ND STAGE

15:42.000 --> 15:42.630
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF

15:42.630 --> 15:43.930
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF
It was so good.

15:44.640 --> 15:47.750
I think it's more interesting than
when I read it in the novel.

15:48.110 --> 15:49.680
Really?

15:49.680 --> 15:50.200
Yes, it is.

15:51.240 --> 15:53.130
The most memorable part

15:53.480 --> 15:56.070
was when they found out
why flying dragons can't fly.

15:56.770 --> 16:00.370
I thought it was very human and realistic

16:00.370 --> 16:01.650
that Chris was scared.

16:02.120 --> 16:04.650
Do you think so?

16:05.280 --> 16:06.530
What do you mean?

16:06.970 --> 16:10.160
Oh, nothing.
Is there anything else?

16:10.500 --> 16:15.000
I also liked the development
of the story after that.

16:16.040 --> 16:18.170
I like that part too!

16:18.790 --> 16:21.320
After that, Libra suggested to Chris,

16:21.320 --> 16:25.760
"Let's ride the flying dragon together
and see the outside world together!"

16:36.180 --> 16:36.590
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF

16:36.590 --> 16:40.690
Chris was scared to see
the world by herself.

16:41.140 --> 16:41.940
Yes.

16:42.320 --> 16:45.690
But with Libra, she could fly.

16:46.090 --> 16:50.200
She wanted to fly out into the sparkling
outside world, but she was afraid,

16:50.630 --> 16:55.950
and it was Libra who took Chris
out of the box of being all alone.

16:56.280 --> 17:00.460
I am sure that the view she saw
from there changed her.

17:00.860 --> 17:04.210
The gray landscape that Chris
had been seeing until then.

17:05.420 --> 17:06.230
KIND DOC STANDS ALONE

17:06.230 --> 17:08.369
Ever since I was a little girl,

17:08.369 --> 17:11.319
I felt that the scenery
I could see was gray.

17:15.000 --> 17:16.130
What's wrong?

17:16.940 --> 17:17.640
Umm...

17:18.180 --> 17:21.310
What is Libra best at?

17:22.589 --> 17:24.119
I think that he's being able

17:24.430 --> 17:28.069
to say straightforwardly what he thinks.

17:28.600 --> 17:31.800
This script is not just fiction.

17:32.070 --> 17:32.660
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF

17:32.660 --> 17:35.030
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF
It is the story of Kikuchi herself.

17:39.170 --> 17:41.750
Do you want to know about Hinami?

17:42.130 --> 17:42.810
Yes.

17:43.370 --> 17:45.080
I want to know in order

17:45.450 --> 17:48.340
to learn a little deeper about
Arcia's human nature.

17:48.640 --> 17:50.680
Arcia's human nature...

17:51.310 --> 17:54.680
Libra is clumsy, Chris is scared,

17:54.680 --> 17:58.100
but Arcia is just strong
and has no "weakness."

17:58.520 --> 18:00.060
The more I wrote,

18:00.060 --> 18:02.100
the more I began to wonder about it.

18:02.520 --> 18:03.600
Wonder?

18:04.280 --> 18:08.460
I wondered how Arcia
could stay so strong.

18:13.590 --> 18:16.240
I'm kind of nervous
about this interview.

18:16.540 --> 18:17.900
Well, then, Kikuchi.

18:18.310 --> 18:18.980
Yes.

18:19.510 --> 18:20.520
Umm...

18:20.520 --> 18:25.220
What is the reason why you are trying
so hard to do so many things, Hinami?

18:26.220 --> 18:28.530
However, the interview

18:28.960 --> 18:30.390
was a mere sham conversation

18:30.740 --> 18:33.420
with no real opinion from Hinami herself.

18:34.330 --> 18:39.110
Surely, there were no answers that Kikuchi
wanted to incorporate into her work.

18:40.870 --> 18:45.020
Hinami was probably telling a lie.

18:46.220 --> 18:48.470
No matter how I connected the words,

18:48.470 --> 18:51.290
I couldn't see the motive
behind her actions.

18:51.750 --> 18:54.620
She didn't intend to tell us the truth.

18:55.550 --> 18:57.320
So, Arcia is probably

18:57.660 --> 19:00.860
not just trying his best because
he is driven by his environment

19:00.860 --> 19:03.680
and his duty.

19:04.580 --> 19:08.790
There must be something out there.

19:09.400 --> 19:10.560
I think so too.

19:11.280 --> 19:13.050
But I still don't know what it is.

19:13.640 --> 19:15.980
Even I, who know her other side,

19:16.510 --> 19:17.570
don't know about it yet.

19:19.270 --> 19:20.010
Kikuchi,

19:20.720 --> 19:24.250
do you want to find out
a little bit more about Hinami?

19:25.890 --> 19:27.900
HAKUSHAKU-TEI 24 HOURS

19:30.250 --> 19:31.430
I am Maebashi,

19:31.700 --> 19:33.400
nice to meet you.

19:33.700 --> 19:34.710
I am Tomozaki,

19:35.030 --> 19:36.280
nice to meet you.

19:37.060 --> 19:38.770
I am K-Kikuchi,

19:38.770 --> 19:40.360
nice to meet you.

19:41.320 --> 19:43.920
Alright, I want to start right away.

19:44.310 --> 19:46.920
Ah, by the way,
I have Hinami's permission.

19:47.320 --> 19:48.420
So,

19:48.850 --> 19:51.530
Tachibana is in the same
junior high school as Hinami?

19:51.530 --> 19:52.150
Yep.

19:52.570 --> 19:56.890
And the one who is in the same
elementary school is Maebashi?

19:56.890 --> 19:58.050
That's right.

19:58.550 --> 20:01.110
Then, from junior high school first.

20:01.110 --> 20:04.060
Tachibana, is there anything
memorable about Hinami?

20:04.360 --> 20:06.360
What I remember is

20:06.870 --> 20:10.310
that she was dating the vice president
of the boys' basketball club.

20:10.310 --> 20:11.980
Eh?! Really?

20:12.390 --> 20:14.930
He was a very popular
and cool senior back then.

20:15.320 --> 20:18.490
But Hinami dumped him right away.

20:18.760 --> 20:21.350
She must have stood out for a long time...

20:22.370 --> 20:24.370
Not really.

20:24.370 --> 20:25.870
What do you mean?

20:26.490 --> 20:31.500
I don't think she stood out
in elementary school.

20:31.800 --> 20:33.500
Is that so?

20:33.500 --> 20:36.510
I got the impression that she was
a serious, cheerful, and good girl.

20:36.870 --> 20:38.330
And, of course,

20:38.330 --> 20:41.390
she has a good family.

20:41.390 --> 20:43.260
Yes, that's true.

20:43.660 --> 20:48.020
I have the impression that she loved
her younger sisters very much.

20:48.480 --> 20:49.230
Sisters?

20:50.120 --> 20:52.420
Hinami had a sister?

20:53.110 --> 20:55.290
Well, please say hello to Hinami for me.

20:56.810 --> 20:58.320
Thanks for everything!

21:02.010 --> 21:03.320
What's wrong, Tachibana?

21:04.100 --> 21:08.000
Maebashi said earlier that Hinami
had younger sisters, right?

21:08.000 --> 21:09.710
Yes, she did.

21:09.710 --> 21:11.670
If that's the case, it's weird.

21:12.750 --> 21:16.710
Because Aoi only has one sister.

21:17.820 --> 21:19.590
Are you sure about that?

21:20.070 --> 21:22.470
Yes, I'm sure of it.

21:26.440 --> 21:29.210
I don't think it's something
we should pursue too far.

21:29.840 --> 21:32.290
At least, if Hinami hasn't said anything.

21:33.000 --> 21:34.110
I agree.

21:34.460 --> 21:35.690
Let's stop it

21:36.760 --> 21:38.140
right here.

21:41.990 --> 21:42.360
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF

21:42.360 --> 21:45.490
THE WAY TO FLY I KNOW NOT OF
I was able to fix the Arcia scene,

21:46.040 --> 21:49.830
but I still haven't worked on the scene
where Chris flies away with Libra.

21:50.650 --> 21:51.550
Don't worry.

21:52.080 --> 21:54.500
We'll be able to practice for the first half.

21:59.260 --> 22:01.260
VACANT CLASSROOM A
IN USE

22:03.370 --> 22:04.760
T-Then!

22:06.300 --> 22:09.210
I'd like to start practicing
reading the script!
